    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>(Prerequisite: Ravenloft Campaign)</em></p><p>Your shadow is alive and always with you, and sometimes it acts on its own will. You gain the following features.</p><p><strong>Grasping Shadow.</strong> You learn the @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplMageHand00]{Mage Hand} cantrip, and you can cast it without components. Your spellcasting ability for this spell is Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma (chosen when you take this feat).</p><p><strong>Lengthened Strike.</strong> When you make a melee attack roll as part of the Attack or Magic action on your turn, you can increase your reach for that attack by 10 feet as your shadow stretches out to help. You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Ominous Will.</strong> Immediately after you roll a 1 on the d20 of a D20 Test, your shadow tries to impose its will. Make a Wisdom saving throw (DC 13 plus your Proficiency Bonus). On a failure, you have the &amp;Reference[Incapacitated] condition until the start of your next turn; when that turn begins, roll on the Shadow's Will table to determine what you do during it.</p><h4>Shadow's Will</h4><table><thead><tr><th>1d8</th><th>Behavior</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>You take no action or Bonus Action, and you spend all your movement moving in a direction determined by 1d4: 1, north; 2, east; 3, south; 4, west.</td></tr><tr><td>2–6</td><td>You don't move or take a Bonus Action; you take the Attack action and make one melee attack against a random creature within your reach. If none is within reach, you take no action.</td></tr><tr><td>7–8</td><td>You have the &amp;Reference[Prone] condition, and your turn ends.</td></tr></tbody></table><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-L83ztSpWVydQtEHZ\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p><em>Lengthened Strike</em> spends a use of the feat. <em>Ominous Will</em> is a Wisdom saving throw against DC 13 + your Proficiency Bonus; on a failure, apply its effect (Incapacitated). <em>Shadow's Will</em> rolls the table.</p></section>",
